{"type":"message","id":"355fe1a4","parentId":"4f417ad5","timestamp":"2026-05-18T09:07:39.654Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_Qa0I5dI8IfTvofKwrbF2ansK","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"story_id\": \"crypto-liquidations-bitcoin-ether-2026-05-18\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Crypto market selloff triggers massive liquidations in Bitcoin and Ether\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"crypto liquidations\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Crypto traders betting on a rally lose $563 million in liquidations as Ether and Bitcoin lead losses\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"Bitcoin\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"bitcoin\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinDesk\",\n    \"Google News\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://www.coindesk.com/markets/2026/05/18/crypto-traders-betting-on-a-rally-lose-usd563-million-in-liquidations-ether-and-bitcoin-suffer-the-most\",\n    \"https://news.google.?oc=5\",\n    \"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivwFBVV95cUxPaFB0VnhqRmROaDR3M0w5S2c5RmU0WW9UcFQwUkJFRDJvRXU1Z3VQU2RNaVBRZDlCSFNmQWNTNi12SEl6Z2xrRjJ2Mkp6cUN2LUdFdjJsbDNoc0FDVnRiWE5oancycjZKcmpPQ28xdXJweG9Gb0ZFd01ZaU9pdFpxdjB4RHZ2ZGE1c1Zxay1tVDEzNWgwcFVVLXRBSDNlZUFSdWF4UmFXdlRDTUZ2ZVlpQkZkRlloMXJaMnV3X3U4Yw?oc=5\",\n    \"https://news.google.?oc=5\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"CoinDesk\\u2019s feed summary says crypto traders betting on a rally lost $563 million in liquidations, with Ether and Bitcoin suffering the most.\",\n    \"A Google News item mirroring Bloomberg\\u2019s coverage says Bitcoin hit a two-week low as crypto liquidations topped half a billion.\",\n    \"Other same-day related headlines describe Bitcoin falling to about $76.7K and say the selloff triggered roughly $661 million in liquidations, reinforcing that leveraged longs were the main casualty.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"On Mon, 18 May 2026, the dominant crypto news event across the feeds was a sharp market selloff that triggered a large wave of liquidations, with Bitcoin and Ether leading the damage. CoinDesk\\u2019s feed headline was explicit: \\u201cCrypto traders betting on a rally lose $563 million in liquidations. Ether and bitcoin suffer the most.\\u201d Its summary said Ether and bitcoin led liquidations as their prices dropped on macroeconomic concerns. Another CoinDesk item published the same morning framed the move as \\u201cBitcoin slides under $77,000 as oil shock and Treasury yields hit risk assets,\\u201d adding context that long-term holders were still sitting tight and exchange balances remained near six-year lows, while underwater short-term holders left BTC vulnerable.\\n\\nThe same event was echoed in Google News results from multiple outlets. One headline read: \\u201cBitcoin (BTC) Hits Two-Week Low as Crypto Liquidations Top Half a Billion - Bloomberg.com.\\u201d Another same-day result said: \\u201cBitcoin falls to two-week low of $76.7K as crypto market selloff triggers $661 million liquidations - The Economic Times.\\u201d A further related headline said: \\u201c$660M Liquidated as Bitcoin Crashes on Trump-Iran Escalation Fears - CryptoPotato.\\u201d Yet another reported: \\u201cToday in Crypto: Bitcoin Price Dips to $76K, Ethereum Leads $650M Liquidation Flush on Weekend - The Crypto Times.\\u201d The Google News feed also surfaced a separate but closely related story: \\u201cCrypto traders betting on a rally lose $563 million in liquidations. Ether and bitcoin suffer the most - CoinDesk,\\u201d confirming that the liquidation theme was being widely covered by multiple outlets on the same day.\\n\\nThe related headlines point to a common pattern: leveraged longs were getting wiped out as risk assets sold off together. The CoinDesk summary says the drop was tied to macroeconomic concerns, while another CoinDesk headline linked the move to oil shock and Treasury yields. The Google News results show the broader press framing it as a market-wide risk-off move, with Bitcoin making a fresh two-week low and liquidations ranging from \\u201chalf a billion\\u201d to roughly \\u201c$661 million\\u201d depending on the source and timestamp.\\n\\nA separate Google News cluster also included the CoinDesk piece itself as a mirrored item and a Bloomberg item focused on Bitcoin\\u2019s two-week low. Taken together, the coverage shows a unified market narrative: traders who were positioned for a rebound were forced out, Ether and Bitcoin were hit hardest, and the liquidation cascade became the biggest crypto market event of the day.\\n\\nThe extracted text available from the RSS layer is limited, but the feed snippets consistently describe the same event: a broad crypto downturn, heavy liquidations, Bitcoin under pressure near the mid-$70,000s, and Ether among the worst performers. CoinDesk\\u2019s wording emphasizes the size of the wipeout and the fact that traders betting on a rally bore the brunt. Google News adds corroborating headlines from Bloomberg, The Economic Times, CryptoPotato, and The Crypto Times, all pointing to the same high-volatility selloff and its liquidation consequences.\"\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779095259654}}
