{"type":"message","id":"4ef8bf72","parentId":"e3604616","timestamp":"2026-05-18T09:15:40.507Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] I checked the actual run, and the main reason is clear:\n\n### Why the chart was not included\n\n1. **The chart generation step failed validation**\n   - The chart agent returned `CHART_DONE: /tmp/chart.png`\n   - But validation immediately failed with: **`CHART_INVALID: not a PNG`**\n   - After that, the pipeline **deleted `/tmp/chart.png`** and continued.\n\n2. **The article still contains raw chart placeholders**\n   - `/tmp/crypto-article.md` still has **2 occurrences** of:\n     - `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]`\n\n3. **The DOCX export only added the feature image**\n   - The export step used:\n     - `![Feature Image](/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg)`\n   - It did **not** replace `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]` with an actual image reference for the chart.\n\n4. **At publish time, the chart file no longer existed**\n   - I verified:\n     - `/tmp/chart.png exists = False`\n\n### So the real diagnosis\n\nThe Google Doc did not include charts because:\n\n- the chart file was **invalid**\n- the pipeline **removed it**\n- the article placeholders were **never converted into actual chart image embeds**\n- the DOCX builder only embedded the **feature image**, not the chart\n\n### In short\n\nThis run failed for **both** reasons:\n- **chart generation failed**\n- **DOCX export logic does not currently inject charts into the placeholders**\n\n### Best fix\n\nI’d recommend changing the pipeline so that before `pandoc` runs, it:\n\n- checks whether `/tmp/chart.png` is valid\n- replaces each `[CHART_PLACEHOLDER]` in a temporary export file with markdown like:\n  - `![Price Chart](/tmp/chart.png)`\n- if the chart is invalid/missing, either:\n  - remove the placeholders, or\n  - fail the publish step instead of silently continuing\n\nIf you want, I can patch the pipeline so future Google Docs include the chart correctly."}]